  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "﻿Redevelopment\r\nto provide part 2/part 3 storey building comprising of 9 terraced\r\ndwellinghouses (Class C3), parking, landscaping, bin and cycle stores, and all\r\nassociated works (amended application form, documents and plans)",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed development would not\r\nprovide adequate usable private amenity space for the future occupiers of the proposed\r\ndevelopment, particularly having regard to the family-sized level of occupation\r\nfor the majority of the proposed dwellings. The gardens would be north-facing, four\r\nplots would measure only 4m deep, all with 1.8m high boundary fencing. It is\r\nconsidered the amenity spaces would be deficient in natural light, be\r\novershadowed for much of the day, failing BRE standards for eight of the nine\r\nproposed dwellings and, so, be compromised in terms of size and usability. In\r\nthis way, the quality of the external amenity space is considered sub-optimal,\r\ncontrary to Policy GR1(B) of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;By\r\nvirtue of the proposed siting of the dwellings, particularly Plots 1-6 with a\r\nseparation distance significantly below the typically expected 21m distance, together\r\nwith the height and scale of the proposed dwellings (particularly Plots 4-6 at\r\nthree-storeys) and continuous line of massing, the proposed development would result\r\nin an unacceptable adverse impact upon the amenities of neighbouring properties\r\nto the north and south by reason of overbearing appearance and visual\r\ncontainment. The front and rear second floor to Plots 4-9 would result in undue\r\nactual or perceived sense\r\nof overlooking and loss of privacy to neighbouring properties. The proposal would be contrary to Policy\r\nD3.D of the London Plan (2021) and Policy GR1\r\nof the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-pagination:widow-orphan&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed soft landscaping scheme,\r\ntree retention and incompatible tree replacement as shown, taking account of\r\nthe quantum of the trees, their siting in relation to the proposed development\r\nand the spatial constraints of the site and mixed function required of the\r\nnarrow footpath and area to the front of the dwellings, would likely be\r\nunrealistic and unsustainable and ultimately result in a poor design of development.\r\nThis is considered to be contrary to the provisions of Policies N2 and N3 of\r\nthe NPPF (2026), Policy G7 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy G14 (Part I) of\r\nthe Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The site is located within Surface\r\nWater Flood Zones 3b (high) &amp;amp; 3a (medium) and is also within a Critical\r\nDrainage Area. In the absence of details relating to the existing and finished\r\nground levels and given that compensatory flood storage would be required for\r\nany loss of floodplain, the application fails to demonstrate that the proposed\r\ndevelopment would be safe from flooding or that it would or demonstrate\r\nappropriate measures to manage the risk of flooding. In addition, the proposed\r\ndrainage strategy is unsatisfactory and inaccurate given it is not possible to\r\ndischarge to a combined water sewer in Harrow. The proposals are therefore considered\r\ncontrary to Policy F7 of the NPPF (2026), Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the\r\nLondon Plan (2021) and Policy CN3 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
